        "Content": "Hume Auctioneers- We Get The Pick Of The Crop\n\nOwner occupied and substantailly upgraded, this beautiful and spacious home offers an excellent opportunity to acquire a quality home in a relaxing and quiet setting within walking distance of all amenities.\n\nThis extra spacious own-door ground floor apartment enjoys a super location at Riverview, Ashgrove in the heart of Mountmellick.\n\nThe property sits in a quiet and peaceful setting on the ground floor and facing an attractive private greenspace.\n\nWith newly fitted energy-efficient windows and a beautiful composite front door, the property has achieved an impressive B-rated BER. This means greater comfort, lower energy bills and it also qualifies for a highly competitive lower interest rate green mortgage.\n\nThe welcoming entrance hall announces a home of great space.\n\nThere is a large kitchen dining room which enjoys great space and a large patio door which floods the property with natural light and access to the green area.\n\nThere are two excellent double bedrooms and a third room which could serve as a home office, playroom or extra storage to compliment the already excellent storage.\n\nA large bathroom completes the accommodation.\n\nThe property is owner occupied and in exceptionally good condition.\n\nAshgrove is a highly sought-after residential location within walking distance of Mountmellick town centre. The property is conveniently positioned close to a wide range of local amenities including shops, supermarkets, cafés, schools, churches, and sporting facilities.\n\nMountmellick is a thriving town with a strong community feel and continues to grow in popularity due to its affordability and accessibility. There is alarge Super Valu within walking distance and a new Lidl set to open in the coming months.\n\nThe property enjoys excellent connectivity, with easy access to the N80, providing direct routes to Portlaoise, Tullamore, and Carlow. Portlaoise, with its mainline rail station and access to the M7 motorway, is approximately a 15-minute drive, making this an ideal commuter base."
